From 1257c8431f192fe2c5650f17b0ac304077cc0d91 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: raold <868138+raold@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:05:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] List idle randombots in the Raid Browser

Randombots only copy Dungeon Finder queues that real players are in, and the
raid browser is not a queue, so it stayed empty. A world-thread check now keeps
a rotating set of idle randombots per faction listed for raids of their level
and expansion, dropping each listing when it expires or the bot is invited.

Opt-in via Playerbots.RandomBotJoinRaidBrowser (default off), with
RandomBotRaidBrowserListings and RandomBotRaidBrowserListTime.
---
 conf/playerbots.conf.dist      |  14 ++++
 src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp | 147 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.h   |   4 +
 src/PlayerbotAIConfig.cpp      |   3 +
 src/PlayerbotAIConfig.h        |   3 +
 5 files changed, 171 insertions(+)

